Rule 13 (If the output tuple is specified, it should contain two tensors, and the output of the min must be an input)
{v_1 : tuple(tensor), v_2 : tensor} |= if ∃i ∈ [0, v_1.len - 1] : v_1[i] = v_2 then v_1.len = 2
>>
Rule 14 (If input tensor has size 0 along the reduction dimension, reduction dimension must be specified)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= if shape(v_1, v_2) = 0 then (v_2 ≥ (-1 * ndim(v_1)) ∧ v_2 < ndim(v_1))
>>
Rule 15 (When comparing two tensors, if dimension 'dim' is specified, the size of v1 and v2 along that dimension v3, must be equal)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : int} |= if v_3 ≥ (-1 * ndim(v_1)) ∧ v_3 < ndim(v_1) then shape(v_1, v_3) = shape(v_2, 0)
>>
Rule 16 (when dim is specified, keepdim must be a boolean)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int, v_3 : bool} |= (v_2 ≥ (-1 * ndim(v_1)) ∧ v_2 < ndim(v_1)) ∧ (v_3 = true ∨ v_3 = false)
>>
Rule 17 (If the two input tensors have different numbers of dimensions, their last dimensions must match)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) ≠ ndim(v_2) then shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 1) = shape(v_2, ndim(v_2) - 1)
>>
Rule 18 (v_2 is within the boundary of v_1)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_2) - 1] : shape(v_2, i) ≤ shape(v_1, i)
>>
